## Viewing History: Where Did This Change Come From?

```bash
git log --oneline          # Simple one-line commit list
    
# Detailed view:
    - Short SHA (first 7 characters)
      Author name & email  
      
        Commit date
      
              Full message describing the change.
```

Branches let you work on different features simultaneously—create a branch, add changes and test there; later merge back to main.

## Undo Mistakes Safely

Git makes it easy:

```bash
# Discard uncommitted staged files:
  git restore --staged filename   // Unstage only
    
    # Also unstages completely unreferenced file versions.
     ```
     
